<title>USA: Ventritex difibrilator approved by FDA.</title>
<headline>Ventritex difibrilator approved by FDA.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ventritex Inc said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration granted it premarket approval for commercial distribution of its Contour implantable cardioverter defibrillators, the V-145D and the LT V-135D, to treat abnormally rapid heart beats.</p>
<p>It said its defibrillators are the smallest available and are designed to enhance patient comfort and facilitate implantation.</p>
<p>The company said availability will be limited initially, but &quot;we are working to increase production to accommodate anticipated demand.&quot;</p>
</text>
